# 002_alignment — pairwise whole-genome alignment + SV calling (minimap2 + SyRI)

Aligns 9 Capsella-clade genomes pairwise and calls structural variants with
SyRI. Each *C. bursa-pastoris* (Cbp) assembly is split into its Co and Cr/Cg
subgenomes, and pairs are only made **within** a homeolog set (Co set,
Cr/Cg set). Implements ANALYSES_INVENTORY.md B1 items #2 (SyRI across key
pairs), and provides the inputs for #7 (SV polarization) and #9 (diploid
baseline). See repo-root `CLAUDE.md` for genome/cluster/software background.

## Genomes (data/genomes.tsv)

`name  fasta_path  n_chrom  group  ref_mode`. Sources are the same 9 genomes as
`001_edta`. Only the `n_chrom` longest sequences are kept (chromosomes; unplaced
scaffolds, organelles dropped).

| name | source | chr | ref_mode |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cbp2-2 | this project's Cbp assembly | 16 | `given` |
| Co39 | this project's Co assembly | 8 | `diploid` |
| Cr145 | this project's Cr assembly | 8 | `diploid` |
| CbpChinese | GCA_036452645.1 | 16 | `fixed_cbp` |
| CbpRussian | GCA_001974645.2 | 16 | `cbp` |
| CgMosher | *C. grandiflora* Mosher RAM v1.1 | 8 | `diploid` (Cr set) |
| CoMosher | *C. orientalis* Mosher RAM v1.1 | 8 | `diploid` |
| CrMosher | *C. rubella* Mosher RAM v1.1 | 8 | `diploid` |
| CoRussian | *C. orientalis* Russian | 8 | `diploid` |

## Rules this analysis follows

- **Source genome files are never modified.** Everything is derived into
  `results/` (copies). Sequence **names are never changed** in the outputs.
- **Subgenome membership is given where known, not inferred.** Cbp2-2's
  subgenomes are the existing `Cbp2-2Co_…`/`Cbp2-2Cr_…` FASTAs
  (`data/subgenome_files.tsv`); `ref_mode=given` skips alignment entirely.
- Any chromosome-level decision (subgenome, homolog number, orientation) is
  recorded in `results/01_norm/<name>.chrmap.tsv`.

### How each genome gets its subgenome / orientation (`ref_mode`)

| ref_mode | genomes | subgenome from | homolog no. + strand from |
|---|---|---|---|
| `given` | Cbp2-2 | source subgenome FASTAs | rank within subgenome file; strand `+` (no alignment) |
| `diploid` | Co39, Cr145, CoMosher, CoRussian, CrMosher, CgMosher | the genome itself | minimap2 vote vs Co39+Cr145 |
| `fixed_cbp` | CbpChinese | `data/subgenome_fixed.tsv`: authors' A set (CP144183-190) = Cr, B set (CP144191-198) = Co | vote vs the same subgenome of Cbp2-2 |
| `cbp` | CbpRussian | minimap2 vote vs Cbp2-2 Co+Cr | same vote |

Why not vote everywhere: a whole-chromosome vote is unreliable for Cbp chr2
(Cbp2-2 SCF_2 splits ~50/50 between Co and Cr — likely homeologous exchange).

**CbpChinese A=Cr / B=Co is an evidence-based call, not a given.** Neither
diploid reference separates its A set (both ~0.4-0.5 aligned coverage). Against
Cbp2-2's own subgenomes A prefers Cr and B prefers Co on all 16 chromosomes
(margins ~0.05-0.15 coverage), and each chromosome then matches its Cbp2-2
counterpart 1:1 (support 0.91-0.98). Revisit if a stronger subgenome marker
becomes available.

Reverse-complemented chromosomes (`-` strand vs the reference, so SyRI doesn't
call whole-chromosome inversions): CbpRussian CM069049.1 (Co chr7) and
CM069050.1 (Cr chr7), CoRussian O4 (chr7). All other chromosomes are `+`.

## Pairs (data/pairs.tsv)

30 pairs = all 15 pairs within each set:

- Co set (order): Co39, Cbp2-2Co, CbpChineseCo, CbpRussianCo, CoMosher, CoRussian
- Cr set (order): Cr145, Cbp2-2Cr, CbpChineseCr, CbpRussianCr, CrMosher, CgMosher

In every pair, **ref = the genome earlier in the set order** (diploid
reference first), so SV direction (INS/DEL, dup/loss) is consistent for
polarization. Cbp2-2Co/Cr are in 10 of the 30 pairs.

## Pipeline

Conda env `syri_1.8.2` (syri 1.8.2, plotsr 1.2.0, minimap2 2.31, samtools,
seqkit). Smoke test: `scripts/test_env.sh`.

1. **`000_prep_genomes.sh`** (array 1-9) — trim headers to the first token,
   keep the `n_chrom` longest sequences (fails if any kept sequence < 10 Mb).
   → `results/00_prep/<name>.fa`
2. **`001_chrom_normalize.sh`** (array 1-9, two waves — see `submit_all.sh`) —
   builds `results/01_norm/<name>.chrmap.tsv` (qchrom, subgenome, homolog chr,
   strand, support_frac, aligned_bases) per `ref_mode`, requires a clean 1:1
   assignment, then writes the per-subgenome FASTAs syri consumes
   (`<name>.fa`, or `<name>Co.fa` + `<name>Cr.fa` for Cbp) with original names.
   Wave 2 (`cbp`, `fixed_cbp`) needs `Cbp2-2.chrmap.tsv` from wave 1.
3. **`002_align_syri.sh`** (array 1-30, 16 CPUs) — per pair:
   `minimap2 -ax asm10 --eqx` → BAM (in `$TMPDIR` only) → `syri -F B` →
   per-pair `plotsr` figure. → `results/02_syri/<ref>_vs_<qry>/`
   (`*.syri.out`, `*.syri.summary`, `*.syri.vcf`, `*.plotsr.png`).
4. **`003_summarize.sh`** (+ `003a_summarize.py`) — → `results/03_summary/`:
   - `sv_summary.tsv` — every row of every `syri.summary` (long)
   - `pair_metrics.tsv` — per pair: genome sizes, syntenic / not-aligned bp and
     fractions, inversion/translocation/duplication counts, SNP/indel counts
   - `sv_size_filtered.tsv` — counts and bp of SVs >= 50 bp and >= 1 kb from
     `syri.out` (INV, TRANS, INVTR, DUP, INVDP, NOTAL ref/qry, INS, DEL)
   - `Co_chain.png`, `Cr_chain.png` — chained 6-genome plotsr figures

## Running

```
cd scripts
bash submit_all.sh          # 000 -> 001 (2 waves) -> 002 -> 003, afterok chain
```

Single pair for a test: `sbatch --array=1 002_align_syri.sh`; override with
`sbatch --export=ALL,PRESET=asm20,OUTROOT=../results/02_syri_test ...`.
Logs land in `scripts/std/`.

## Choices and caveats to keep in mind

- **Preset `asm10` for all 30 pairs.** Pilots on Co39 vs Cbp2-2Co and Cr145 vs
  CgMosher (the most divergent pair, ~0.9% syntenic SNP density): asm10 aligned
  more than asm20, lost nothing, ran faster. **Translocation/duplication counts
  are preset-dependent** (~30-100% higher under asm10, from alignment
  fragmentation); inversions and coverage are stable. Compare raw SV counts
  only within this one run, and prefer `sv_size_filtered.tsv` for comparisons.
- `syri.summary` "Insertions/Deletions/SNPs" are within-alignment small variants,
  **not** comparable to the dnadiff SV counts in the manuscript's Fig 1.
- Assembly size differences inflate one-sided numbers: 8-chromosome totals range
  from ~123 Mb (CoRussian) to 181 Mb (CoMosher) in the Co set and 125 Mb
  (CbpRussianCr) to 213 Mb (CgMosher) in the Cr set. Read unaligned/duplication
  totals against `pair_metrics.tsv` genome sizes.
- BAMs are not kept (regenerable; bigdata is nearly full).
- `syri` 1.8.2 has no `--tmpdir`; `--dir` chdirs, so paths passed to it are absolute.

## First look at the results (preliminary — not tested)

From `pair_metrics.tsv` (SNPs per kb of syntenic reference sequence):

- All 30 pairs align sensibly (syntenic fraction 0.46-0.99). The lowest are
  the Cbp-vs-CgMosher pairs, driven by CgMosher's larger assembly.
- Within-species diploid pairs are the closest: Co39/CoMosher/CoRussian
  0.8-1.2 SNP/kb; Cr145 vs CrMosher 4.2.
- Cbp2-2 and CbpRussian look similar to each other (Co 3.0, Cr 3.7 SNP/kb),
  closer than either is to the diploid references (Co39 vs Cbp2-2Co 4.6).
- **CbpChinese is consistently the most diverged Cbp** in both subgenomes
  (Co: 8-10 SNP/kb against the other Cbps, 10 vs Co39; Cr: ~9-10 vs other Cbps,
  12-18 vs Cr145/CrMosher/CgMosher) and its subgenomes are larger (Co 167 Mb,
  Cr 164 Mb vs 127-141 / 126-135 Mb for the others). This could be a genuinely
  distinct lineage/donor, or assembly/partitioning effects — undecided; it bears
  directly on the single- vs multiple-origin question, so treat as a lead only.
- Several large inversions appear specific to single Cbp assemblies in the chain
  plots (e.g. Cr set SCF_7 ~11-19 Mb, CbpChineseCr vs both Cbp2-2Cr and
  CbpRussianCr; Cr set SCF_2 near CbpChineseCr). Biology vs misassembly not
  separated here.
- Not yet done: check unaligned/diverged regions against the `001_edta` TE
  annotation (are they repeats?), SV polarization (#7), diploid baseline (#9).

## Outputs

```
data/         genomes.tsv  pairs.tsv  subgenome_files.tsv  subgenome_fixed.tsv
results/
  00_prep/<name>.fa
  01_norm/<name>[Co|Cr].fa(.fai)   <name>.chrmap.tsv
  02_syri/<ref>_vs_<qry>/          syri.out / .summary / .vcf / plotsr.png
  03_summary/                      sv_summary.tsv pair_metrics.tsv sv_size_filtered.tsv {Co,Cr}_chain.png
```
